  "term": "paranoid personality disorder",
  "definition": "Paranoid personality disorder is a personality disorder marked by an unwarranted belief that other people are hostile or harmful. It commonly shows up as suspiciousness, mistrust, hypersensitivity, and a tendency to avoid accepting blame that is deserved.",
